>> title: Massaman Curry Paste
>> category: Spice Blends & Marinades
>> tags: thai, cinnamon, paste, chiles, curry
>> counters: Thai Kitchen
>> aka: prik gaeng massaman, gaeng massamun paste, matsaman paste, mussaman curry paste, massaman paste, massamun paste
>> pairs-with: massaman-curry
>> servings: 8
>> time: 1 hr
>> slack: narrow — the spices burn while the aromatics are still pale, so the two minutes and the ten never happen in the same pan

>> step: soak 20 min, drain and chop
Soak @dried long red chiles{8}(stemmed and seeded) in hot water for ~soak{20%min}, then drain and chop them.

>> step: toast 3 min, grind in a mortar
Toast @coriander seeds{1%Tbs}, @cumin seeds{2%tsp}, @green cardamom pods{5}(cracked), @cloves{5}, @cinnamon stick{1}(broken up) and @star anise{1} in a dry #skillet{} over medium heat for ~toast{3%min}, until the cardamom smells of camphor, then grind them to a powder in a #mortar{}.

>> step: char 10 min, then peel
Char @shallots{5}(unpeeled) and @garlic{10%cloves}(unpeeled) in the same dry #skillet{} over medium-high heat for ~roast{10%min}, turning them until they blacken in patches and soften, then peel them.

>> step: pound to a fibrous paste
Pound @&(~3)soaked chiles{} and @&(~1)charred shallots and garlic{} with @kosher salt{1%tsp}, @lemongrass{2%stalks}(tender parts only, thinly sliced) and @galangal{1%Tbs}(peeled and chopped) to a fibrous paste.

>> step: work in
Work @&(~3)ground spices{} and @shrimp paste{1%Tbs}(kapi) into @&(~1)paste{}.
